==Enemy==
He has extremely short ranged attacks, but makes up for it with the ability to spawn level 3 [[Wave Attack]] at a 100% chance. Treat him as a stronger [[Kory]] with less standing range that spawns en masse. Do note that the Crazed Gross's Wave Attack reaches a range of 800, meaning only a few cats like [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Nerd Cat]] can avoid the attack.

==Strategy==
If you have [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]], this enemy becomes a cakewalk. He can also be made a cakewalk using any [[:Category:Wave Shield Cats|Wave Blockers]], notably [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]], in combination with tough, durable meatshields such as [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Wall Cat]].

Alternatively, you can avoid meatshields and use plenty of ranged attackers, such as [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cat]] or [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]], as these will eventually stack up and knock him back before he can even attack.

